p-svc-intro.md","line":36},{"title":"Domain support for schedules","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/domain-support-for-schedules.md","line":134},{"title":"Schedule entry fields","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/r_ScheduleEntryFields.md","line":142},{"title":"Assign a maintenance schedule to configuration items","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-service-management/change-management/use-maintenance-schedule-management.md","line":155},{"title":"Conflict detection","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/it-service-management/change-management/c_ConflictDetection.md","line":158},{"title":"Define a schedule","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/t_DefineASchedule.md","line":173},{"title":"Schedule entry fields","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/r_ScheduleEntryFields.md","line":175},{"title":"Parent and child schedules","target":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ServiceNow/ServiceNowDocs/australia/markdown/platform-administration/c_ParentAndChildSchedules.md","line":177},{"title":"Conflict detection","target":"c_ConflictDetection","line":181}],"metadata":{"title":"Create blackout and maintenance schedules in Change Management","description":"Use the Blackout and Maintenance windows to schedule a change. Blackout windows specify times during which normal change activity should not be scheduled. Maintenance windows specify times during which change requests should be scheduled. For example, create a blackout schedule for code freezes at the end of the year. blackout-maintenance-schedule","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-se